{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 2360566,
  "courseSlug": "sveltejs-the-complete-guide",
  "courseTitle": "Svelte.js - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "14689714",
      "title": "Understanding Readable Stores",
      "lectureOrder": 109,
      "videoOrder": 97,
      "sourceHash": "6b359f95b8b078eed01ca8492e27fd7ddc5cec3347579ce647457ebac969e697",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.1,
          "end": 7.53,
          "en": "We had a first look at stores and the Writeable store is by far the most important store.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 7.89,
          "end": 12.51,
          "en": "There also is a readable store though, and it has its use cases as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 13.12,
          "end": 16.36,
          "en": "Let me show you an example here by adding.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 17.56,
          "end": 19.72,
          "en": "A timer storages file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 19.72,
          "end": 21.8,
          "en": "And again, the naming is always up to you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 21.82,
          "end": 27.36,
          "en": "And here I'll import readable from svelte slash store.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 27.37,
          "end": 28.87,
          "en": "So we got readable here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 28.87,
          "end": 30.88,
          "en": "And how does the readable store work now?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 31.62,
          "end": 36.27,
          "en": "You still export either as a default or as here as a named export.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 36.3,
          "end": 39.48,
          "en": "Your store and I'll name that timer again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 39.51,
          "end": 42.15,
          "en": "The name is up to you and you then simply call.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 42.98,
          "end": 44.48,
          "en": "Readable like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 45.47,
          "end": 49.4,
          "en": "Now as before, you can initialize this with a default value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 50.52,
          "end": 52.02,
          "en": "For example, zero.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 52.02,
          "end": 54.6,
          "en": "But that could also be an array, an object, whatever you need.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 55.58,
          "end": 60.38,
          "en": "Unlike the Writeable store, though, the readable store also takes a second argument.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 60.38,
          "end": 62.66,
          "en": "And that is actually a function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 63.38,
          "end": 69.26,
          "en": "That is a function which receives an argument, which itself is a function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 69.26,
          "end": 73.91,
          "en": "You can give it any name you want, but this is a function which will allow you to set a new value for",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 73.91,
          "end": 74.47,
          "en": "the store.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 74.48,
          "end": 76.55,
          "en": "Hence I will name that function set.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 76.67,
          "end": 83.27,
          "en": "And now in that body of the function you are passing as a second argument to readable, you can set",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 83.27,
          "end": 84.53,
          "en": "a new value for the store.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 84.53,
          "end": 89.96000000000001,
          "en": "Now, since it's readable, you can only set values from inside this function from outside.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 89.96000000000001,
          "end": 92.95,
          "en": "You can't now with outside mean that before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 92.96000000000001,
          "end": 99.62,
          "en": "For example here with card item, we were able to update or set our store data right.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 99.62,
          "end": 104.87,
          "en": "We could use our store and call update or set to change the data in the store with a readable store.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 104.9,
          "end": 107.21000000000001,
          "en": "That's not possible on a readable store.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 107.24000000000001,
          "end": 112.82,
          "en": "You will only be able to subscribe The only place where the data in the store can change is from inside",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 112.82,
          "end": 113.66,
          "en": "this function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 113.66,
          "end": 116.12,
          "en": "Now, you might wonder when do we use this?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 116.13,
          "end": 122.22,
          "en": "Well, for example, if you have some form of timer which increments itself, if you have a interval",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 122.22,
          "end": 128.67,
          "en": "or for example, if you have an app where you get the user geolocation there, you also can use a watch",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 128.67,
          "end": 132.48,
          "en": "position to get an ongoing update of the current position of the user.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 132.48,
          "end": 138.48,
          "en": "If you have something like this, you can always store the new position in that store here and read",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 138.48,
          "end": 139.86,
          "en": "from it in your application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 139.86,
          "end": 144.96,
          "en": "You never need to update that position from anywhere else in your application because it is derived",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 144.96,
          "end": 146.67000000000002,
          "en": "automatically here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 146.67000000000002,
          "end": 149.55,
          "en": "I'll not use position, but instead the interval.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 149.91,
          "end": 151.68,
          "en": "So what you can do in here is.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 152.96,
          "end": 155.06,
          "en": "You can call Setinterval.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 156.61,
          "end": 163.78,
          "en": "Choose a time, maybe one second, so 1000 milliseconds, and then you pass a function here to set interval.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 163.78,
          "end": 164.74,
          "en": "That is how it works.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 164.74,
          "end": 170.2,
          "en": "And in there you can now call that set function, which you're getting as an argument passed in automatically",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 170.2,
          "end": 172.87,
          "en": "to that function you're setting as a second argument.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 172.87,
          "end": 179.77,
          "en": "So set is provided to you by svelte, so to say and set allows you to set a new value in your store",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 179.77,
          "end": 180.28,
          "en": "here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 180.95,
          "end": 182.03,
          "en": "Now here to set.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 182.06,
          "end": 188.9,
          "en": "I of course, want to pass an incremented number and for that I will also manage the number itself here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 189.51,
          "end": 191.64,
          "en": "So count starts at zero.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 191.64,
          "end": 193.63,
          "en": "Count is then what I pass in here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 193.65,
          "end": 194.67,
          "en": "Count is Then what?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 194.67,
          "end": 196.68,
          "en": "I increase here with every interval.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 197.53,
          "end": 203.07999999999998,
          "en": "And then the updated count is what I pass here to set back into the store so that whoever subscribes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 203.07999999999998,
          "end": 205.09,
          "en": "to the store gets our updated count.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 207.81,
          "end": 214.14,
          "en": "Now, it's also worth mentioning that you should return a cleanup function here, which is called whenever",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 214.14,
          "end": 215.88,
          "en": "the store is not needed anymore.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 216.69,
          "end": 224.4,
          "en": "For example, here the interval gives us back an identifier which we should store and then here in my",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 224.4,
          "end": 224.86,
          "en": "readable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 224.88,
          "end": 227.52,
          "en": "So in this function I pass as a second argument.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 227.55,
          "end": 233.67000000000002,
          "en": "I return a new function which is called automatically by svelte when this store is not needed anymore.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 233.67000000000002,
          "end": 239.46,
          "en": "And there I'll call clear interval, which is a default JavaScript function where I clear this interval",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 239.49,
          "end": 244.38,
          "en": "again to avoid memory leaks and to make sure that this interval doesn't keep on going even though we",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 244.38,
          "end": 245.58,
          "en": "don't need it anymore.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 246.66,
          "end": 253.05,
          "en": "So now we have our readable store and we can use it in the app world file pretty similarly to how we",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 253.05,
          "end": 254.22,
          "en": "use the Writeable store.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 254.22,
          "end": 260.19,
          "en": "Before though, just with the big exception of course, that we now are limited to subscribing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 260.49,
          "end": 263.85,
          "en": "So here I'll get my timer from the.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 264.54,
          "end": 269.37,
          "en": "Timer store JS file and here I can set up my timer.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 270.11,
          "end": 271.55,
          "en": "And subscribe.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 272.2,
          "end": 279.43,
          "en": "Get my value, my count and I can console log that count and it should increment every second.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 279.43,
          "end": 283.51,
          "en": "And of course, you can also use the dollar sign trick here in the markdown if you want to output it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 283.51,
          "end": 284.08,
          "en": "there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 285.95,
          "end": 286.85,
          "en": "I will show you both.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 286.85,
          "end": 288.65,
          "en": "So first of all, let's save this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 288.65,
          "end": 292.64,
          "en": "And here you see that incrementing number That's looking good.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 293,
          "end": 298.90999999999997,
          "en": "Now, let me actually add app here to make sure that this is coming from the app svelte file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 298.90999999999997,
          "end": 300.86,
          "en": "Let's add the same here in the cart.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 300.86,
          "end": 303.29,
          "en": "So in there I'll import.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 304.92,
          "end": 308.76,
          "en": "Timer from the timer store.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 309.38,
          "end": 311.8,
          "en": "And let's set up a subscription here as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 311.81,
          "end": 314.03,
          "en": "So here I also subscribe.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 314.03,
          "end": 317.6,
          "en": "I get the count and I console log here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 318.84,
          "end": 324.3,
          "en": "And a console log card, too, so that we see that this is coming from the card.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 324.34,
          "end": 329.37,
          "en": "Now, if I save this, you see app one card, one app, two card two.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 329.4,
          "end": 332.97,
          "en": "So they're getting the same values here, so that all works.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 333.87,
          "end": 336.33,
          "en": "Now I'll manually unsubscribe here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 336.42,
          "end": 339.09000000000003,
          "en": "Unsubscribe Like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 342.04,
          "end": 346.21,
          "en": "And bring back on destroy to call.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 346.21,
          "end": 348.4,
          "en": "Unsubscribe when we clear this card.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 348.43,
          "end": 349.93,
          "en": "Now let's save this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 350.08,
          "end": 353.77,
          "en": "And if I now toggle the card, you see that only the app keeps on going.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 353.8,
          "end": 357.94,
          "en": "If I bring back the card, however, it also goes again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 357.94,
          "end": 358.96,
          "en": "Or it starts again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 358.96,
          "end": 365.47,
          "en": "And please note that it starts at the value where the app is so it doesn't start a new timer because",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 365.47,
          "end": 368.14,
          "en": "it's one at the same store with one and the same value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 368.14,
          "end": 369.43,
          "en": "And that is the idea here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 369.43,
          "end": 373.15,
          "en": "It would be bad if every component would get its own copy of the store.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 373.15,
          "end": 379.63,
          "en": "So if I remove the card again, you see the app keeps on going to 2728 and if I now toggle card again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 379.63,
          "end": 383.32,
          "en": "you see the card now also keeps on going at 30, 31 and so on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 383.32,
          "end": 385.36,
          "en": "So that's really important to keep in mind.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 385.39,
          "end": 388.76,
          "en": "They're using the same data source, they're using the same store.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 388.81,
          "end": 390.76,
          "en": "That is the idea behind the store.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 391.06,
          "end": 397.24,
          "en": "Now, last but not least, let me also show you the the trick regarding the auto subscription here in",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 397.24,
          "end": 397.54,
          "en": "App.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 397.54,
          "end": 402.56,
          "en": "If I uncomment this, if I don't set up my subscription like this, but instead I want to output it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 402.56,
          "end": 403.13,
          "en": "here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 404.39,
          "end": 411.35,
          "en": "Cut out a paragraph with count and then simply dollar timer, and this automatically creates a subscription",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 411.35,
          "end": 411.98,
          "en": "to the timer.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 411.98,
          "end": 416.78,
          "en": "And if we would ever get rid of the app component, it would also clear the subscription automatically.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 416.78,
          "end": 423.59,
          "en": "So now with that, yeah, of course we should wrap this in curly braces so that it's not text, but",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 423.59,
          "end": 426.23,
          "en": "treat it as a dynamic JavaScript expression.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 426.23,
          "end": 433.13,
          "en": "But now with that here at the bottom you see that timer for the app or it's the same story but inside",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 433.13,
          "end": 433.61,
          "en": "the app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 433.61,
          "end": 435.74,
          "en": "And here on the right you see the timer in the cart.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 435.77,
          "end": 441.71,
          "en": "Again, both are getting the data from the same store and therefore, just as I showed before, if I",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 441.74,
          "end": 446.42,
          "en": "toggle the cart, you see no logs anymore because we got rid of that subscription.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 446.42,
          "end": 453.05,
          "en": "The app keeps on going, however, but if I bring back the cart, it also starts again at the last value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 453.05,
          "end": 457.43,
          "en": "the app was at because the store kept on going, the store wasn't cleared.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 458.90999999999997,
          "end": 463.11,
          "en": "Now, what if I don't subscribe here in the app and I only have the cart?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 463.14,
          "end": 465.78,
          "en": "However, now you see it starts, of course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 465.78,
          "end": 466.17,
          "en": "Cart.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 466.17,
          "end": 467.1,
          "en": "One, two, three.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 467.13,
          "end": 469.74,
          "en": "If I now clear that it stops.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 469.77,
          "end": 476.31,
          "en": "If I now start again, it still picks up on the value It stopped the last time because the store is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 476.31,
          "end": 477.27,
          "en": "never disposed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
